From 5050c0073f44df77f6799ce2adeeb65a550f8ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:02:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] STEP 15: never issue a 2-D D2H into host memory -- the split
 read is the peer grant, not the arithmetic

The CUDA backend's 2-D read path issued a `hipMemcpy2DAsync` device->host copy of a split tensor's row
block into llama.cpp's pinned output buffer, which ONE device registered and every device of a `-sm
tensor` split reads.  A 2-D D2H copy makes the runtime grant the copying device's agent access to that
allocation, and this box refuses those grants ("Allow p2p access failed - hsa_amd_agents_allow_access
with err 4096"), so HIP returned `invalid argument` and the server aborted:

  E ggml_backend_cuda_get_tensor_2d_async: device 1: 2-D read of 'result_output' failed (invalid
  argument): 331092 bytes x 5 copies, tensor pitch 331092, host pitch 993280, offset 0 (ROCm1 buffer)

It is NOT the Meta backend's split arithmetic: measured at the abort the per-device chunks are
331092 / 331092 / 331096 (uneven by one ELEMENT), summing exactly to the meta row (993280) and to
ggml_nbytes, and device 0's copy of the same arguments -- the allocation's owner -- succeeded.

So the backend no longer issues a 2-D D2H into host memory.  ggml_cuda_rows_to_host() serves a tight
block or a single copy as ONE 1-D copy; a big synchronous block through the device-staged form (2-D
device-to-DEVICE gather into the reading device's own staging buffer, one 1-D D2H per chunk into that
device's own pinned chunk, host scatter); and the ASYNC form (which must not synchronize) or a small
block as one 1-D copy per row.  Both 2-D read entry points use it (the async one, which aborted, and
the buffer's synchronous get_tensor_2d).  Also: the async read now selects its own device (its write
twin already did), and the staged arm can no longer gather a row larger than the 64 MiB staging pair.

This is a DELIVERY-level fix carried by the beta artifact for now: at promotion it is cut into the
delivery on its own (a block-09 amendment) and this patch is dropped from beta/prefill-decode-arms/.

Verified: repro/repro-mtp-prefill.sh survives 3 rounds (prompt_n 77100 served, 415 decode-arm steps,
2 handovers, fd trace 686/688/11); gates/gate-arms-state-split.sh PASS 11/11; gate-arms-{cancel,
fd-budget,default-inert,multislot,spec 36/36} PASS; gate-{ckpt-reuse,state-pipe,meta-seg-drain,
spec-purity,prefill-logits,seqpar} PASS; whole-set all build clean; no GPU fault over the ladder.
Records: WORKLOG.md 261124.007, INVARIANTS.md r384-wip, RUNS.md (2026-11-24 STEP 15).
